      "message": "technically, mScanController can be null anytime.\n\nSo this:\n\n```\nif (mScanController !\u003d null) {\n  mScanController.foo();\n}\n```\ncan lead to a null pointer exception as dump is run on a different thread tha the thread turning on and off the bt.\n\n\nI agree that this is unlikely to happen, but per sake of the murphy law, I would use a temp variable like this:\n```\nScanController scanController \u003d mScanController;\nif (scanController !\u003d null) {\n  scanController.foo();\n}\n```\n\nThis is not fixing the inner method of the ScanController (I haven\u0027t look at this) but it will prevent race cleaning the class variable",
